bility density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}(3{x}^{2}+2x+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426229 1072 #uuid "0ee0de2e-5389-59ac-b881-e7c459d89539" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426229 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 0) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{20}(3{x}^{2}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{[{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}([{0}^{3}+{0}^{2}+0]-[(-2)^{3}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(0-[-8+4-2]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426230 1062 #uuid "24093c17-aaf6-5f14-99d2-b70a36b04680" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426230 1063 #edb/ref 17592186426229 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426231 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426234 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426231 1062 #uuid "aa7621a8-c239-56bc-b82e-cc8333eb035f" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426231 1063 #edb/ref 17592186419853 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426232 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426233 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426232 1062 #uuid "d927fc2b-e4ac-5ab3-9c2f-ee91ca8f7ea8" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426232 1063 #edb/ref 17592186275459 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426233 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426231 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426233 1062 #uuid "dacdef7e-822e-524b-ac66-efc7856bf374" 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426233 1063 #edb/ref 17592186275460 13194139534574 17592186045417 true] [17592186426234 1058 #ed